{"format":"hologram.registry.artifact/v1","id":"mcr.microsoft.com/azurelinux/base/nodejs","fetched":"2026-09-25T12:12:07.858Z","source":{"name":"Microsoft Artifact Registry","api":"https://mcr.microsoft.com/api/v1/catalog/azurelinux/base/nodejs/details?reg=mar","page":"https://mcr.microsoft.com/en-us/product/azurelinux/base/nodejs/about"},"readme":"## About\n\nThis repository contains the official NodeJS image for Azure Linux.\n\n### What is Azure Linux?\n\nAzure Linux is a Linux distribution for Microsoft’s cloud infrastructure and edge products and services. Azure Linux is designed to provide a consistent platform for these devices and services and will enhance Microsoft’s ability to stay current on Linux updates.  \n\nTo learn more about Azure Linux, refer to our [GitHub repository](https://github.com/microsoft/azurelinux/).\n\n### What is Node.js?\n\nNode.js is a platform built on Chrome's JavaScript runtime for easily building fast, scalable network applications. Node.js uses an event-driven, non-blocking I/O model that makes it lightweight and efficient, perfect for data-intensive real-time applications that run across distributed devices.\n\nSee: http://nodejs.org\n\n## Featured tags\n\n- `20`\n\nThe featured tags are multi-architecture tags (i.e., `x86-64` and `aarch64`) that refer to the latest version of the image. Additional tags that are specific to nodejs version, Azure Linux build, or architecture can be found in the Tags section.\n\n## Usage\n\n### Running a simple Node.js app\n\n`1.` Create a Dockerfile to generate a new image that includes the necessary content.\n\n    # For Node.js 20\n    FROM mcr.microsoft.com/azurelinux/base/nodejs:20\n\n    # Copy source files, install app dependencies, and build app.\n    COPY package*.json ./\n    RUN npm install\n    COPY . .\n    RUN npm run build\n\n    # Replace this with your application's default port\n    EXPOSE 8080\n\n    # Start the app with your application's start command.\n    CMD [ \"npm\", \"run\", \"start\" ]\n\n`2.` Build and run your container image.\n\n    docker build -t nodejs-app-image .\n    docker run -it -p 8080:8080 --name running-nodejs-app nodejs-app-image\n\nThe default container startup command is `node`.\n\n### Run a single Node.js script\n\nFor many simple, single file projects, you may find it inconvenient to write a complete Dockerfile. In such cases, you can run a Node.js script (named my-script.js in the example below) by using the Azure Linux based Node.js docker image directly:\n\n    # For Node.js 20\n    docker run -it --rm --name running-nodejs-script -v \"$PWD\":/usr/src/app -w /usr/src/app mcr.microsoft.com/azurelinux/base/nodejs:20 node my-script.js\n\n### Run Node.js repl environment\n\nYou may want to simply run the virtual environment called REPL (READ, EVAL, PRINT, LOOP) that comes with Node.js by launching it when the container starts. In such case, you can run Node by using the Azure Linux based Node.js docker image directly. The following command will launch the virtual environment that Node.js comes with:\n\n    # For Node.js 20\n    docker run -it --rm mcr.microsoft.com/azurelinux/base/nodejs:20\n\n### Launch Azure Linux shell\n\nThe Node.js image ships with a bash shell. The launch command can be provided to docker run command to Launch Azure Linux shell. The following command will launch the shell:\n\n    # For Node.js 20\n    docker run -it --rm mcr.microsoft.com/azurelinux/base/nodejs:20 /bin/bash\n\n## Support\n\nAzure Linux container images are supported only for internal Microsoft use. For more information please see our [Support Statement](https://github.com/microsoft/azurelinux/blob/-/SUPPORT.md).\n\n## License\n\nThe Azure Linux distribution is provided under the [MIT license](https://github.com/microsoft/azurelinux/blob/-/LICENSE). Individual packages and components are governed by their own licenses included in the package sources available via srpm on [packages.microsoft.com](https://packages.microsoft.com/azurelinux/) or via our [GitHub repository](https://github.com/microsoft/azurelinux/).\n\n- Legal Notice: [Container License Information](https://aka.ms/mcr/osslegalnotice)","readmeBase":null,"publisher":{"name":"Microsoft","url":"https://mcr.microsoft.com/","official":true,"verified":true},"registered":null,"updated":"2026-09-16T14:57:16.4909525+00:00","categories":[],"keywords":[],"license":"MIT","links":[],"maintainers":[],"stats":{"pulls":null,"pullsText":"114K+","stars":null},"mediaTypes":[],"contentTypes":[],"storage":null,"tags":[{"name":"24.21","digest":"sha256:9d24caf762eaea25ab6742648553d19ee2b07897d545bd5a9884e6b313546df5","pushed":"2026-09-16T14:38:36.0000000+00:00","size":null,"platforms":[],"mediaType":"application/vnd.docker.distribution.manifest.list.v2+json","status":null},{"name":"24","digest":"sha256:9d24caf762eaea25ab6742648553d19ee2b07897d545bd5a9884e6b313546df5","pushed":"2026-09-16T14:38:32.0000000+00:00","size":null,"platforms":[],"mediaType":"application/vnd.docker.distribution.manifest.list.v2+json","status":null},{"name":"24.21.0-1-azl3.0.20260909","digest":"sha256:9d24caf762eaea25ab6742648553d19ee2b07897d545bd5a9884e6b313546df5","pushed":"2026-09-16T14:38:28.0000000+00:00","size":null,"platforms":[],"mediaType":"application/vnd.docker.distribution.manifest.list.v2+json","status":null},{"name":"24.21.0-1-azl3.0.20260909-arm64","digest":"sha256:10acb589adcf90ac456ba266ae80c9856a72841a59a683b82b5a6e11309722c7","pushed":"2026-09-16T14:38:26.0000000+00:00","size":2008,"platforms":["linux/arm64"],"mediaType":"application/vnd.docker.distribution.manifest.v2+json","status":null},{"name":"24.21.0-1-azl3.0.20260909-amd64","digest":"sha256:ef33b68ec0e22b6855bdaba776a6396324423ba507801ebbcd595b180ebdc22e","pushed":"2026-09-16T14:38:18.0000000+00:00","size":2004,"platforms":["linux/amd64"],"mediaType":"application/vnd.docker.distribution.manifest.v2+json","status":null},{"name":"24.20","digest":"sha256:65efb6be4323d2da4f73531a37d84fff0e451cddc82e4da